      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T11:52:27Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the first exploit receipt and call trace, the proxy creation receipt, complete Upgraded(address) log range from block 17405188 through the exploit block, pre-exploit implementation hash, verified ApeStaking source, pinned reproduction, all successful attacker calls in blocks 17496620-17496648, and historical prices. The exploit executes proxy 0x0b89032e2722b103386adccae18b2f5d4986afa0 and delegates the affected staking functions to 0x85018cf6f53c8bbd03c3137e71f4fca226cda92c. Its sole pre-exploit Upgraded event is creation log 49 and selects that implementation. The defect is NFT/stake ownership accounting, not setCollectRate authorization: setCollectRate only changes the caller's payout preference. After APE flash-loan repayment, the attacker controlled 7.000099 WBTC, 102469.546694 USDT, 6996.324771 USDC, and 4276.679165404022135955 APE; protocol calls also paid 190.744764897999370387 gross ETH before gas. DefiLlama's closest high-confidence observations value these assets at $629,929.32."
